 hippocampus in long-term memory: is it memory store or comparator?</article-title><source>J Integr Neurosci</source><volume>7</volume><fpage>117</fpage><lpage>184</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18431820</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005265-Cipolotti1"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cipolotti</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Bird</surname><given-names>CM</given-names></name></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Amnesia and the hippocampus.</article-title><source>Curr Opin Neurol</source><volume>19</volume><fpage>593</fpage><lpage>598</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17102699</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005265-Viskontas1"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Viskontas</surname><given-names>IV</given-names></name><name><surname>Carr</surname><given-names>VA</given-names></name><name><surname>Engel</surname><given-names>SA</given-names></name><name><surname>Knowlton</surname><given-names>BJ</given-names></name></person-group><year>2008</year><article-title>The neural correlates of recollection: Hippocampal activation declines as episodic memory fades.</article-title><source>Hippocampus</source><volume>19</volume><fpage>265</fpage><lpage>272</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18830998</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005265-Kircher1"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kircher</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Weis</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Leube</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Freymann</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Erb</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2008</year><article-title>Anterior hippocampus orchestrates successful encoding and retrie